{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"3dd1b775ef213d20170eb0edce21540ff0637421bac6b00b58ebfc38dc8fd930","digest":{"component_or_area":"async push mechanism and e2e test suite","key_entities":["src/rebar/_store/push.py","tests/interfaces/store/test_push_policy_e2e.py","git push","PYTHONPATH","start_new_session","close_fds","DEVNULL"],"problem_keywords":["async push","detached child","parent exit","survival","e2e test","test coverage gap"],"propositions":["The detached async-push child process (spawned with start_new_session=True, close_fds=True, DEVNULL streams) must survive and complete its push after the parent CLI process exits.","Current e2e test polls origin while parent stays alive, proving in-process completion but not parent-exit survival.","A controlled git wrapper shim is needed to block git push behind a release file and emit an 'entered push' marker so test ordering is deterministic.","Test must launch rebar create with async push in subprocess, confirm parent exits while child remains blocked, then release and verify the event/commit arrives on origin.","The test does not re-cover spawn-failure logging or PUSH_PENDING surface semantics (already tested elsewhere)."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785822318090489078,"uuid":"c654d3fc-f7aa-4ca3-a301-2617cc645664"}